In article <44059@dime.cs.umass.edu> picquend@unix1.cs.umass.edu (Marc Picquendar) writes:
>In article <1992Feb27.001456.18887@beaver.cs.washington.edu> pullen@cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:
>>Suggested new item: A ring (or amulet) of curse resistance. While
>>wearing this, it will prevent any of your items from being cursed by
>>magic using monsters, such as liches, nagas, titans, shamans, demon
>>lords, and of course the Wiz. Perhaps it could be set up so that
>>nothing in your inventory can change its blessed/curse status while
>>you are wearing, so you would have to remove it before you can get any
>>effects from remove curse or holy water.
>
>This ring should be curseable, suppose you put a cursed one on, then it
>sticks for the rest of the game and you cannot curse/uncurse anything
>- even the ring itself -

Sure you could get rid of it: Just zap a wand of lightning at yourself
a few times until it disintegrates :) But yeah, I get your point. The
ring of curse resistance should work like a luckstone. A *blessed*
ring will prevent anything from ever being cursed in your inventory,
although you can still uncurse and bless. An uncursed ring will
prevent anything from changing status period, as above (or maybe it
should allow you to still unbless/uncurse items, but not curse/bless
them). A *cursed* ring will prevent you from ever blessing anything
(although you can still uncurse items like the ring itself).

